pkg/proc, service/api: detsched.node and detsched.start, channels in one line, on print labels

detsched.node was the name package sim gives a node's handle, such as
"n2 (start 4)", so cond NAME detsched.node == "n2" never held. It is now
the node's name, "n2", and detsched.start which start of the node the
goroutine runs in, 4 (0 for no node). The position on stops and hits
still names both: "node n2 (start 4)".

A channel printed as the runtime's whole hchan wherever structs print
in several lines, as print and on NAME print do in the terminal: its
buffer, element type, wait queues, lock and synctest bubble, about 25
lines a hit. It prints in one line now, with its length, capacity,
whether it is closed, and, in that multi-line form, the address of its
hchan:

	chan int 3/100 (closed) at 0xc000123000

The one-line form elsewhere, as in the JSON output and DAP, is
upstream's with " (closed)"; the JSON value record has the address in
"addr". *ch, which was refused, is the hchan, and prints it whole;
ch.closed and the other fields read as before.

on NAME print EXPR labelled the value with the name evaluation gave
its result, so a field read through an interface field, j.env.err,
printed as "data.err", in text and in the JSON record's "expr", where
stock Delve 1.27.2 does the same in text. The value is now labelled
with EXPR.

detsched.node and detsched.start are detsched's (0003); the rest are
generic fixes for upstream Delve.

diff --git a/pkg/proc/detsched.go b/pkg/proc/detsched.go
